  "notes": "{濁|にご}る has two distinct meanings: liquid becoming cloudy, and consonants becoming voiced.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{濁|にご}す→濁す：19579_nigosu⟧ (transitive - to make muddy; to mumble)\n\nSENSE 1 - CLOUDY/MUDDY:\nDescribes liquid losing clarity.\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{濁|にご}る: water becomes cloudy\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{濁|にご}る: eyes become clouded\n- ⟦{声|こえ}→声：02207_koe⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{濁|にご}る: voice becomes muddy/unclear\n\nSENSE 2 - VOICED (LINGUISTICS):\nDescribes consonant voicing (adding ⟦{濁点|だくてん}→濁点：27818_dakuten⟧):\n- か→が, さ→ざ, た→だ, は→ば\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- ⟦{濁点|だくてん}→濁点：27818_dakuten⟧: voicing mark (゛)\n- ⟦{濁音|だくおん}→濁音：19295_dakuon⟧: voiced sound\n- ⟦{清音|せいおん}→清音：23458_seion⟧: unvoiced sound\n- ⟦{濁|にご}り→濁り：13431_nigori⟧: muddiness, cloudiness\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {濁|にご}っている: is cloudy / is muddy (resultative state)\n- Note: {濁|にご}る is a change-of-state verb, so the ている form expresses the resulting state of being cloudy or muddy rather than the process of becoming so. ⟦{川|かわ}→川：02186_kawa⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{濁|にご}っている means \"the river water is muddy\" (as a current condition).",
